        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>The Wraith triggered it, then responded, then the new target entered play next to her. &nbsp;It would still be the To be Continued. . . stage of the turn, so I could see where the argument could be made. &nbsp;But I don&#39;t think the intent is to have a target entering play cause a hazard attack, even in that bizarre circumstance.</p><p>I would go with no, but an official ruling is needed.</p><p>The counterattack would occur.</p><p>This is how timing of Bitter Spiral, Kinetic Redistributor and Synaptic Interuption was explained during playtesting:</p><p>The first attack is defended, and dice are blocked. &nbsp;You then reapply those dice (or roll the attack for Bitter Spiral) and roll for defense on all appropriate targets. &nbsp;Once all attack and defense stemming from dice being blocked is calculated, resolve all the damage.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It is possible (unlike SotM) for characters to incap each other in this way.</p>",
